  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes between the lotteries. The individual's report does not mention any pairwise differences in outcomes or their sum. Instead, the individual focuses exclusively on the probability of winning, concluding that the higher chance in B outweighs the lower expected value or smaller potential gains. Therefore, the information relevant to the decision reason is absent from the report. Furthermore, the individual's justification (based on winning probability) does not align with the rule of the decision reason (which involves summing outcome differences). There is no reference to differences in outcomes or their aggregation. Hence, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
